{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/797001-vampire-investigation-thoughts","id":797001,"title":"Vampire Investigation Thoughts","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-12-30T13:37:01-08:00","id":797001,"title":"Vampire Investigation Thoughts","content":"Understanding that these things need not be codified and that this idea is more looking at guidelines to help a storyteller decide how many Clues uncovering something might require, I thought it might be fun to brainstorm a couple of ways to use the Investigation system in Vampire. I don't mean for highly specific mysteries like &quot;What New York's Ordo Dracul secretly do in Staten Island&quot; but more general stuff, like &quot;Where is Joe The Ventrue's Haven?&quot; which might be a bit more involved than casually looking up that information.<br /> <br /> So I'll start with that example! If anybody else has similar ideas or thoughts, like suggested avenues of investigation for other Kindred-like things, I'd love to hear them. <hr /><b>Finding Someone's Haven</b><br /> <b>Recommended # of Clues: </b>2-3<br /> <b>Potential Clues</b><ul><li>Where is this Kindred's territory in the Domain?</li> <li>Who does she feed on?</li> <li>What is her Covenant?</li> <li>Who are her Allies? Do they act as proxies? Does she own things through them?</li> <li>Who are her Coterie? What do they know?</li> <li>Does she have any kind of mortal connection to this place?</li> <li>Where does she go in her territory?</li> </ul><b>Suggested Modifiers: </b>She's in Your Covenant (+1), Higher City Status (-1), Higher Covenant Status (-1), Anonymity Merit (-1 to -3), Occultation (-1 to -3), Unaligned (-2), No allies or coterie (-1), Nomad (-1)<br /> <br /> Otherwise I'd use the modifiers in the section for investigations in CofD.<br /> <br /> <b>Complications</b><ul><li>She discovers that you found out where her Haven is.</li> <li>She retaliates against you for investigating, threatening territory, blood dolls or other assets.</li> <li>She poisons your reputation with a secret she found from a Harpy, possibly giving you notoriety.</li> <li>She sics mortal investigators, hunters or proxies such as the police or a street gang on you and your allies.</li> </ul>These are just some thoughts. Feel free to add on any suggestions you might have.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-30T15:11:03-08:00","id":797034,"title":"","content":"I feel there should be something for having extra Touchstone and overall using Touchstones greatly, and something for abandoning your Touchstones and rarely visiting them. <br /> It would reinforce the idea that Touchstones are also a potential weakness, which is an interesting angle.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-30T17:16:37-08:00","id":797085,"title":"","content":"As a complication she might have proves that you investigated to find out where she was dwelling and publicly accuse you to seek to destroy her (a serious offense to the Traditions) or worse to commit Diablerie on her. After all for what purpose other than murder or Diablerie a Vampire would want to know where another kindred rests ? ^^","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1851-jps","name":"JPS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"209"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-30T23:33:49-08:00","id":797215,"title":"","content":"Finding someone's bane came up in one of my games. Also, discovering an elder's original name or history. Or are you looking for potential clue ideas?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5220-mother-s-love","name":"Mother's Love","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5220_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"58"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-31T03:36:57-08:00","id":797262,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/797001-vampire-investigation-thoughts?p=797034#post797034\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I feel there should be something for having extra Touchstone and overall using Touchstones greatly, and something for abandoning your Touchstones and rarely visiting them.<br /> It would reinforce the idea that Touchstones are also a potential weakness, which is an interesting angle.</div> </div> </div> </div> Considering that touchstones can be something physical, like a gravestone, instead of something alive, that might be hard to do.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-31T14:11:30-08:00","id":797502,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/797001-vampire-investigation-thoughts?p=797262#post797262\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Considering that touchstones can be something physical, like a gravestone, instead of something alive, that might be hard to do.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Doesn't really hold up... If a gravestone is his touchstone, then if he visits it often, he can be tracked using it... if he doesn't, then he's abandoning his Touchstone <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-31T19:04:10-08:00","id":797587,"title":"","content":"Not to mention even that Touchstone is not unassailable. The grave or corpse can be defiled, his memory of the peson tarnished or insulted and so on.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Politeness is the lubricant of social intercourse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/272-saibot","name":"saibot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar272_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1063"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-31T19:16:48-08:00","id":797593,"title":"","content":"Yeah, but it's a lot less dramatic to mess with something like that than say kidnapping an actual person that reminds you what being human means.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-01T03:53:26-08:00","id":797742,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/797001-vampire-investigation-thoughts?p=797593#post797593\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, but it's a lot less dramatic to mess with something like that than say kidnapping an actual person that reminds you what being human means.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> It should be as dramatic for the vampire as an actual human. Taking non-human touchstones is not an easy way off the &quot;dramatic moments&quot;. If it's less dramatic for you/your group - such touchstones should not be used. (unless you don't care for touchstones/and dramatic moments from them, in taht case, knock yourself out)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-01T07:27:59-08:00","id":797801,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Griautis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/797001-vampire-investigation-thoughts?p=797502#post797502\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Doesn't really hold up... If a gravestone is his touchstone, then if he visits it often, he can be tracked using it... if he doesn't, then he's abandoning his Touchstone <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div> Meh. A vampire can be tracked from his Herd, or a favorite Hunting Ground just as easily. Hell, an Obfuscated vampire can just follow a target home from an Elysium visit. There are far easier methods of tracking than a gravestone you might need to stake out every night for weeks.<br /> <br /> Defiling could severely piss off a vampire that had it as a touchstone, but that's on the level of a grave (no pun intended) insult. Not at all the same thing as a Touchstone lover.<br /> <br /> All that is beside the point I'm making anyways. The point is that the wildly various kinds of touchstones makes forming any kinds of specific rules for Touchstones-as-Clues difficult. They're simply too different from each other to make enough assumptions to form cohesive rules.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-01T08:00:16-08:00","id":797816,"title":"","content":"I know it is almost derailing the thread, but I would like to point to the movie <i>Pulp Fiction</i> and the part about Butch and his father's gold watch. <i>That </i>is what a vampire with a non-person Touchstone is like. Someone messing with their shit is not just &quot;a grave insult&quot;. People can do some crazy shit for things they care about, even if those things are not other people.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Politeness is the lubricant of social intercourse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/272-saibot","name":"saibot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar272_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1063"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-01T13:47:17-08:00","id":797955,"title":"","content":"What saibot said... It doesn't matter what it is... You can't compare it as an &quot;object of value&quot; and &quot;a lover&quot; for a human counterparts. Of course, for a human, most of the time, the lover will be more important. But we're talking touchstones here. They are of utmost importance. They are worth killing for (if the specific vampire kills for touchstones). maybe even dying for (if the specific vampire would die for his touchstones). Taking a non-human touchstone just means that you will fight to preserve what's yours. <br /> <br /> if you'd sacrifice your right arm to save your lover, you would do so for the grave too, because it's a touchstone. The level of attachment is the same from the point of the vampire. If the attachment is not strong enough, then the object should not qualify as a touchstone in the first place.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}